From 09764ed38089ebd234ba3e82a2d642fe26c73ce7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 06:21:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 195/307] perf: LPV RSM draw calls - decouple re-render from
 heartbeat, cull tiny casters

The RSM shadow pass is the only draw call source of the LPV stage
(~600+ casters per render). Two reductions plus one correctness fix:

- RSM re-render is now decoupled from the relight heartbeat: it only
  happens on sun changes, camera movement past ~2 near cells, invalid
  history, or a slow content-refresh fallback (4 heartbeats, catches
  doors/vehicles/streaming). A stationary camera renders ZERO RSM draw
  calls while the grid keeps relighting (bounce feedback) from the last
  rendered RSM.
- Correctness fix this depends on: the injection matrices are now
  pinned at RSM render time (NotifyRsmRender -> UpdateFrameParameters
  only on render frames). Previously they were recomputed every frame
  from the camera-following frustum, so any relight on a frame without
  an RSM render would have injected with matrices disagreeing with the
  stored texels.
- r_LPVRsmMinCasterSize (default 0.5m): objects with a smaller bounding
  radius are skipped by the RSM render - sub-texel props cannot produce
  meaningful bounce surfels, they only cost draw calls.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tu9cj9ax1mqCV93HVfCfpW
